# Resources

## moko-resources

`:shared:common-resources` uses moko-resources 0.26.0. Generated accessor: `MR` in package `dev.nonoxy.residetrack.common.resources`.

Asset locations under `src/commonMain/moko-resources/`:
- `base/strings.xml` — all localizable strings.
- `base/colors.xml` — DS color tokens (read by `ResideTrackTheme`).
- `fonts/` — font files (e.g. `NotoSans-Regular.ttf`).
- `images/` — image files (require `@{n}x` scale suffix for Android drawables, e.g. `icon@1x.png`).

**Basenames must be identifier-safe** — moko mirrors them verbatim:
- `NotoSans-Regular.ttf` → `MR.fonts.notosans_regular`
- `icon@1x.png` → `MR.images.icon`

## Accessing Resources

In `@Composable` context: `stringResource(MR.strings.x)` from `moko-resources-compose`.

In non-Composable context (e.g. `Ui*LabelMapper`): inject `StringConverter` (`:shared:common`) and call `converter.convert(MR.strings.x)`.

`StringConverter` resolves moko `StringResource` → `String` outside Composition. Implementation is platform-actual — on Android it holds `Context`.

## Adding Strings

All strings go in `:shared:common-resources/src/commonMain/moko-resources/base/strings.xml`. No per-feature string files.

## Presentation with MR

`:shared:feature-X:presentation` does NOT get `common-resources` auto-wired by `kmpFeatureSetup`. If a presentation module needs `MR` (e.g. `UiXLabelMapper` resolves strings), add manually:

```kotlin
// <feature>/presentation/build.gradle.kts
commonMainDependencies {
    implementations(projects.shared.commonResources)
}
```

## Code Rules

- String literals in `Text(...)` composables: forbidden — use `stringResource(MR.strings.x)`.
- `Color(0x...)` literals: forbidden — use `ResideTrackTheme.colors.*` tokens.
- Never construct CDN/file URLs on the client for resources managed by the backend.
